      ":question/problem": "A study shows how the sports preferences of young people in a certain community vary from year to year. The following table shows the results of this study. \n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Baseball** | **Basketball** | **Football** |\n| To: | **Baseball** | $0.8$ | $0.2$ | $0$ |\n| **Basketball** | $0.1$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ |  |\n| **Football** | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |  |\n\nFor example, $10%$ of people who used to prefer baseball now prefer football. \n\nGiven that $1\\,260$ young people were interviewed for the study and that the probabilities listed remain constant for many years, how many of those people will eventually prefer baseball?"
